<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Sforza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1401">1401</a>–<a href="/years/1466">1466</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Sforza was an Italian condottiere, son of Muzio Attendolo Sforza, who married Bianca Maria, daughter of Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/filippo-maria-visconti">Filippo Maria Visconti</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. After the duke's death in 1447 he commanded the army of the Golden Ambrosian Republic, then turned against it and entered Milan as duke in 1450, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-sforza">Sforza dynasty</a>. He joined the Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> of 1454, while his brother Alessandro became lord of Pesaro.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-sforza.jpg" alt="Francesco Sforza" width="320" height="514" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: School of Lombardy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francesco_Sforza.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
